From: codeandsolder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: mdio: ipq4019: stop restoring MDC divider per transfer

The Wave 7 MDIO failure was traced to the external QCA8081 reference
clock being disabled during reset, not to the controller's MDC divider.
The PCS-owned CCF refclock model now keeps that clock valid and repeated
hardware trials show stable Clause 22/45 access.

Drop the downstream-style divider rewrite before every MDIO transfer and
return to the upstream transaction behavior. Keep the existing divider
programming at probe and after bus reset unchanged.

Signed-off-by: codeandsolder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/mdio/mdio-ipq4019.c
+++ b/drivers/net/mdio/mdio-ipq4019.c
@@ -85,8 +85,6 @@
 	"uniphy1_phy_ref_clk",
 };
 
-static int ipq4019_mdio_set_div(struct ipq4019_mdio_data *priv);
-
 static int ipq4019_mdio_wait_busy(struct mii_bus *bus)
 {
 	struct ipq4019_mdio_data *priv = bus->priv;
@@ -107,13 +105,6 @@
 	if (ipq4019_mdio_wait_busy(bus))
 		return -ETIMEDOUT;
 
-	/* Qualcomm downstream restores the configured MDC divider before
-	 * every transaction. Keep that behavior so mode changes cannot leave
-	 * the controller running with a stale divider.
-	 */
-	if (ipq4019_mdio_set_div(priv))
-		return -EINVAL;
-
 	data = readl(priv->membase + MDIO_MODE_REG);
 
 	data |= MDIO_MODE_C45;
@@ -155,13 +146,6 @@
 	if (ipq4019_mdio_wait_busy(bus))
 		return -ETIMEDOUT;
 
-	/* Qualcomm downstream restores the configured MDC divider before
-	 * every transaction. Keep that behavior so mode changes cannot leave
-	 * the controller running with a stale divider.
-	 */
-	if (ipq4019_mdio_set_div(priv))
-		return -EINVAL;
-
 	data = readl(priv->membase + MDIO_MODE_REG);
 
 	data &= ~MDIO_MODE_C45;
@@ -194,13 +178,6 @@
 	if (ipq4019_mdio_wait_busy(bus))
 		return -ETIMEDOUT;
 
-	/* Qualcomm downstream restores the configured MDC divider before
-	 * every transaction. Keep that behavior so mode changes cannot leave
-	 * the controller running with a stale divider.
-	 */
-	if (ipq4019_mdio_set_div(priv))
-		return -EINVAL;
-
 	data = readl(priv->membase + MDIO_MODE_REG);
 
 	data |= MDIO_MODE_C45;
@@ -243,13 +220,6 @@
 	if (ipq4019_mdio_wait_busy(bus))
 		return -ETIMEDOUT;
 
-	/* Qualcomm downstream restores the configured MDC divider before
-	 * every transaction. Keep that behavior so mode changes cannot leave
-	 * the controller running with a stale divider.
-	 */
-	if (ipq4019_mdio_set_div(priv))
-		return -EINVAL;
-
 	/* Enter Clause 22 mode */
 	data = readl(priv->membase + MDIO_MODE_REG);
 
